#*'''1979''', {{w|Chris de Burgh}}, ''The Devil's Eye''
#*:I have '''blacked out''' your television, every station in the world is mine.
# {{idiom|intransitive}} To [[lose]] [[consciousness]]; to suffer a [[blackout]].
# {{transitive}} To make a [[room]], [[building]], etc. dark by turning out [[light]]s, drawing [[curtains]], etc., for instance in time of an [[air raid]].

